# Terminal pages with the fallback on-screen keyboard (task 014 P4b). The CLI tile opens the native terminal on the
# harness' fake PTY (no process: the scene prints what the shell would; the fake echoes the keys as a tty and a shell
# would, ^C gives "^C" and a new prompt, ^D "exit" and the end). APPLAUNCH_OSK=auto: the keyboard follows the
# launcher's policy (scene command "keyboards N"). Shots:
#   term_keyboard  a physical keyboard is present: no on-screen keyboard, the whole grid
#   term_osk       the last keyboard went: the on-screen keyboard comes up for the whole session, the grid keeps the
#                  rows above it with the prompt on its last row (the lines above went to the scrollback), the PTY is
#                  resized to them
#   term_123       "ls " typed on it, the 123 layer
#   term_symbols   "-la " typed, the #+= layer
#   term_typed     "ls -la | grep a" typed, back on the letters
#   term_ctrl      Ctrl armed (one-shot)
#   term_ctrl_c    Ctrl then c: ^C (0x03) reached the shell, a new prompt; Ctrl is off again
#   term_restored  a physical keyboard is back: the on-screen keyboard goes, the lines come back, the PTY full size
#   term_exit      the on-screen keyboard back up; Tab, Up, Esc tapped (bytes in the log), then Ctrl+D: the shell
#                  exits, "Press any key to exit" with the keyboard still up (two taps on a key go home)
#   ssh_session    the SSH form: its keyboard's Enter through Host, Port and User connects; the SSH session (the same
#                  terminal page) with the keyboard
# ptylog writes what reached the PTY: every key as bytes (Tab \x09, Up \e[A, Esc \e, ^C \x03, ^D \x04), the sizes.
# Review only: no golden.
title terminal with the on-screen keyboard
review
env APPLAUNCH_OSK auto
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
keyboards 1
home
launch CLI
ptyprompt "pi@zero7:~$ "
ptyout "Linux zero7 6.12.47 aarch64\n\npi@zero7:~$ ls\nDesktop    Music      apps\nDocuments  notes.txt  bin\npi@zero7:~$ uptime\n 20:30:12 up 2 days, 1 user\npi@zero7:~$ df -h /\nFilesystem  Size  Used Use%\n/dev/root    29G  6.1G  23%\npi@zero7:~$ "
shot term_keyboard
keyboards 0
wait 600
shot term_osk
tapkey l
tapkey s
tapkey SPACE
tapkey 123
shot term_123
tapkey -
tapkey abc
tapkey l
tapkey a
tapkey SPACE
tapkey 123
tapkey "#+="
shot term_symbols
tapkey |
tapkey abc
tapkey SPACE
tapkey g
tapkey r
tapkey e
tapkey p
tapkey SPACE
tapkey a
shot term_typed
tapkey Ctrl
shot term_ctrl
tapkey c
shot term_ctrl_c
keyboards 1
wait 600
shot term_restored
keyboards 0
wait 600
tapkey Tab
tapkey UP
tapkey Esc
tapkey Ctrl
tapkey d
wait 300
shot term_exit
tapkey x
tapkey x
wait 600
launch SSH
wait 300
tapkey ENTER
tapkey ENTER
tapkey ENTER
wait 600
ptyprompt "pi@remote:~$ "
ptyout "Linux remote 6.1.0-26-amd64 x86_64\nLast login: Sun Oct 11 18:02\npi@remote:~$ "
shot ssh_session
ptylog pty
